    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add a token-authenticated HTTP/WebSocket remote server in the Tauri backend so the desktop app can be controlled over the network\n- Introduce a web bridge layer (`src/bridge/*`) that lets the existing UI run in a browser when connected remotely\n- Add Settings UI to enable/disable remote access, manage the access token, and copy connection URLs\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Build and run the desktop app locally\n- [ ] Enable remote access in Settings and verify a token + URL are shown\n- [ ] Open the remote URL in a browser with the token and confirm the UI loads\n- [ ] Exercise core flows over remote (PTY, invoke commands, events) and confirm blocked window-only commands stay unavailable\n- [ ] Disable remote access and confirm the server stops and browser sessions disconnect\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
