      "created_at": "2026-09-02T15:16:36Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-02T15:16:37Z",
      "body": "thanks for putting this together @namphamdev \r\n\r\nRemote access is something I want in MonoCode, and this is a useful spike.\r\n\r\nI\u2019m not going to merge it as-is though. Getting this right is a lot bigger than serving the current desktop UI in a browser. The desktop shell is built around Tauri (windows, dialogs, native chrome, the full IDE layout), and remoting that over HTTP/WebSocket turns every invoke into a network API. That\u2019s hard to secure and harder to maintain, and it still doesn\u2019t work well on a phone.\r\n\r\nI am open to brainstorm about this first in an issue/discussion! I am thinking a small host protocol, and a separate companion UI meant for mobile (running agents, follow-up, inbox) rather than a squeezed copy of the desktop app.\r\n\r\nReally appreciate the work but i will need to close this PR. Let's open a discussion on this and move from there",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
